From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:02:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/56] Add JSON tools: Format, Minify and Validate

For .json tabs and untitled tabs starting with { or [, the Edit menu
gets Format JSON (Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F, indent = tab width in spaces),
Minify JSON (Ctrl+Alt+Shift+M) and Validate JSON. A small tokenizer
copies strings and numbers byte for byte, so key order and number text
stay exactly as written; no new dependency. Format and Minify are one
undo step and keep the cursor on the same token. Invalid JSON (JSONC
comments and trailing commas included) is left alone and a bar above
the editor names line, column and reason, with Go to. Texts over 20 MB
are refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

